<title>CANADA: ALPINE SKIING-KATJA SEIZINGER WINS WOMEN'S WORLD CUP DOWNHILL.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-KATJA SEIZINGER WINS WOMEN'S WORLD CUP DOWNHILL.</headline>
<dateline>LAKE LOUISE, Canada 1996-11-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Katja Seizinger won the women's World Cup downhill in Lake Louise, Alberta, on Saturday.</p>
<p>Seizinger finished in 1 minute 41.91 seconds. France's Carole Montillet was second in 1:42.51, Sweden's Pernilla Wiberg third in 1:42.64 and Picabo Street of the United States was fourth in 1:42.68.</p>
</text>
